{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794312459284,"sessionID":"ses_e3aab1ef3ffebz5QUGa5OqEy34","part":{"id":"prt_1c55b53f9001zjS8bvketxGM8H","messageID":"msg_1c55b3e8a0010qL06GMWJMaz1U","sessionID":"ses_e3aab1ef3ffebz5QUGa5OqEy34","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794312459284,"sessionID":"ses_e3aab1ef3ffebz5QUGa5OqEy34","part":{"id":"prt_1c55b53fc001SZ2LcN6xZurU0c","messageID":"msg_1c55b3e8a0010qL06GMWJMaz1U","sessionID":"ses_e3aab1ef3ffebz5QUGa5OqEy34","type":"text","text":"Done. Built the weather display app on top of the existing skeleton.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): full JSON API with SQLite persistence under `./data`, bearer-token auth (register/login/sessions), weather CRUD with server-set `observed_at` and case-insensitive city uniqueness, paged listing, city search that records lookups, and recent-lookups endpoint. Six sample reports seeded on first start.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Tailwind (v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`). Sign-in/register forms, signed-in username + sign-out, city search with weather card or \"No weather data\" message, °C/°F toggle, recent lookups (clickable), and a signed-in-only report manager with add/edit forms showing validation errors and delete-with-confirm.\n\nVerified end-to-end: all API routes return correct statuses/shapes (auth 401s, validation messages, uniqueness, 204 deletes), frontend builds cleanly, and the Flask server serves both `/api` and the built assets. Docker isn't available in the sandbox, so I couldn't run the image, but the app runs via `gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app` and `npm run build` both pass.","time":{"start":1794312459260,"end":1794312459263}}}
